[{"id":"qatala-3-144-12","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijen je","en":"he/it was killed"},{"bs":"ubili ste","en":"you (all) killed"},{"bs":"ubio si","en":"you killed"},{"bs":"i ubijte ih!","en":"and (you all) kill them!"}],"ref":"3:144","answerWord":"قُتِلَ","answerSound":"audio/c5055af683d8c3152ce5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Muhammad is but a messenger, messengers (the like of whom) have passed away before him. Will it be that, when he dieth or is slain, ye will turn back on your heels? He who turneth back on his heels doth no hurt to Allah, and Allah will reward the thankful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَمَا","مُحَمَّدٌ","إِلَّا","رَسُولٌ","قَدْ","خَلَتْ","مِن","قَبْلِهِ","ٱلرُّسُلُ","أَفَإِي۟ن","مَّاتَ","أَوْ","قُتِلَ","ٱنقَلَبْتُمْ","عَلَىٰٓ","أَعْقَٰبِكُمْ","وَمَن","يَنقَلِبْ","عَلَىٰ","عَقِبَيْهِ","فَلَن","يَضُرَّ","ٱللَّهَ","شَيْـًٔا","وَسَيَجْزِى","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ"],"marked":[12],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-191-0","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"i ubijte ih!","en":"and (you all) kill them!"},{"bs":"i ubijaju","en":"and they kill"},{"bs":"ubijate","en":"you (all) kill"},{"bs":"pa ubijte!","en":"so (you all) kill!"}],"ref":"2:191","answerWord":"وَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/8de2847fac8da44ffafb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And slay them wherever ye find them, and drive them out of the places whence they drove you out, for persecution is worse than slaughter. And fight not with them at the Inviolable Place of Worship until they first attack you there, but if they attack you (there) then slay them. Such is the reward of disbelievers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","حَيْثُ","ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ","وَأَخْرِجُوهُم","مِّنْ","حَيْثُ","أَخْرَجُوكُمْ","وَٱلْفِتْنَةُ","أَشَدُّ","مِنَ","ٱلْقَتْلِ","وَلَا","تُقَٰتِلُوهُمْ","عِندَ","ٱلْمَسْجِدِ","ٱلْحَرَامِ","حَتَّىٰ","يُقَٰتِلُوكُمْ","فِيهِ","فَإِن","قَٰتَلُوكُمْ","فَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","كَذَٰلِكَ","جَزَآءُ","ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-4-29-16","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijate","en":"you (all) kill"},{"bs":"ubio sam","en":"I killed"},{"bs":"i ubijeni su","en":"and they were killed"},{"bs":"ubili ste","en":"you (all) killed"}],"ref":"4:29","answerWord":"تَقْتُلُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/dc5117d7fcce66b2f2b5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"O ye who believe! Squander not your wealth among yourselves in vanity, except it be a trade by mutual consent, and kill not one another. Lo! Allah is ever Merciful unto you.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["يَٰٓأَيُّهَا","ٱلَّذِينَ","ءَامَنُوا۟","لَا","تَأْكُلُوٓا۟","أَمْوَٰلَكُم","بَيْنَكُم","بِٱلْبَٰطِلِ","إِلَّآ","أَن","تَكُونَ","تِجَٰرَةً","عَن","تَرَاضٍ","مِّنكُمْ","وَلَا","تَقْتُلُوٓا۟","أَنفُسَكُمْ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","كَانَ","بِكُمْ","رَحِيمًا"],"marked":[16],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-3-157-1","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijeni ste","en":"you (all) were killed"},{"bs":"ubijate","en":"you (all) kill"},{"bs":"ubio ih je","en":"he/it killed them"},{"bs":"ubijen je","en":"he/it was killed"}],"ref":"3:157","answerWord":"قُتِلْتُمْ","answerSound":"audio/7da68b45c90ad76213da.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And what though ye be slain in Allah's way or die therein? Surely pardon from Allah and mercy are better than all that they amass.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَلَئِن","قُتِلْتُمْ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","أَوْ","مُتُّمْ","لَمَغْفِرَةٌ","مِّنَ","ٱللَّهِ","وَرَحْمَةٌ","خَيْرٌ","مِّمَّا","يَجْمَعُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-4-66-5","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijte!","en":"(you all) kill!"},{"bs":"ubili smo","en":"we killed"},{"bs":"i ubijaju","en":"and they kill"},{"bs":"ubio ga je","en":"he/it killed it"}],"ref":"4:66","answerWord":"ٱقْتُلُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/380fe942bcb543cb2775.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if We had decreed for them: Lay down your lives or go forth from your dwellings, but few of them would have done it; though if they did what they are exhorted to do it would be better for them, and more strengthening;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَلَوْ","أَنَّا","كَتَبْنَا","عَلَيْهِمْ","أَنِ","ٱقْتُلُوٓا۟","أَنفُسَكُمْ","أَوِ","ٱخْرُجُوا۟","مِن","دِيَٰرِكُم","مَّا","فَعَلُوهُ","إِلَّا","قَلِيلٌ","مِّنْهُمْ","وَلَوْ","أَنَّهُمْ","فَعَلُوا۟","مَا","يُوعَظُونَ","بِهِۦ","لَكَانَ","خَيْرًا","لَّهُمْ","وَأَشَدَّ","تَثْبِيتًا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-5-30-5","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa ga je ubio","en":"and he killed him"},{"bs":"ubijate ih","en":"you (all) kill them"},{"bs":"zar si ubio?","en":"did you kill?"},{"bs":"pa ubijte!","en":"so (you all) kill!"}],"ref":"5:30","answerWord":"فَقَتَلَهُۥ","answerSound":"audio/b1da824c1699d5fbbdc6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But (the other's) mind imposed on him the killing of his brother, so he slew him and became one of the losers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["فَطَوَّعَتْ","لَهُۥ","نَفْسُهُۥ","قَتْلَ","أَخِيهِ","فَقَتَلَهُۥ","فَأَصْبَحَ","مِنَ","ٱلْخَٰسِرِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-5-70-18","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijaju","en":"they kill"},{"bs":"ubijte!","en":"(you all) kill!"},{"bs":"i ubijte ih!","en":"and (you all) kill them!"},{"bs":"ubijeni su","en":"they were killed"}],"ref":"5:70","answerWord":"يَقْتُلُونَ","answerSound":"audio/33c93451445811f059ee.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We made a covenant of old with the Children of Israel and We sent unto them messengers. As often as a messenger came unto them with that which their souls desired not (they became rebellious). Some (of them) they denied and some they slew.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["لَقَدْ","أَخَذْنَا","مِيثَٰقَ","بَنِىٓ","إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ","وَأَرْسَلْنَآ","إِلَيْهِمْ","رُسُلًا","كُلَّمَا","جَآءَهُمْ","رَسُولٌۢ","بِمَا","لَا","تَهْوَىٰٓ","أَنفُسُهُمْ","فَرِيقًا","كَذَّبُوا۟","وَفَرِيقًا","يَقْتُلُونَ"],"marked":[18],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-26-14-5","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubit će me","en":"they will kill me"},{"bs":"ubili su ga","en":"they killed him"},{"bs":"ubili ste","en":"you (all) killed"},{"bs":"ubijam","en":"I kill"}],"ref":"26:14","answerWord":"يَقْتُلُونِ","answerSound":"audio/f405d5a0109f89ec5188.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they have a crime against me, so I fear that they will kill me.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَلَهُمْ","عَلَىَّ","ذَنۢبٌ","فَأَخَافُ","أَن","يَقْتُلُونِ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-54-13","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa ubijte!","en":"so (you all) kill!"},{"bs":"da te ubiju","en":"so that they may kill you"},{"bs":"pa ga je ubio","en":"and he killed him"},{"bs":"ubijate ih","en":"you (all) kill them"}],"ref":"2:54","answerWord":"فَٱقْتُلُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/5b3a648506f036f7b8ce.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when Moses said unto his people: O my people! Ye have wronged yourselves by your choosing of the calf (for worship) so turn in penitence to your Creator, and kill (the guilty) yourselves. That will be best for you with your Creator and He will relent toward you. Lo! He is the Relenting, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَإِذْ","قَالَ","مُوسَىٰ","لِقَوْمِهِۦ","يَٰقَوْمِ","إِنَّكُمْ","ظَلَمْتُمْ","أَنفُسَكُم","بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ","ٱلْعِجْلَ","فَتُوبُوٓا۟","إِلَىٰ","بَارِئِكُمْ","فَٱقْتُلُوٓا۟","أَنفُسَكُمْ","ذَٰلِكُمْ","خَيْرٌ","لَّكُمْ","عِندَ","بَارِئِكُمْ","فَتَابَ","عَلَيْكُمْ","إِنَّهُۥ","هُوَ","ٱلتَّوَّابُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-72-1","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubili ste","en":"you (all) killed"},{"bs":"ubijte!","en":"(you all) kill!"},{"bs":"ubio si","en":"you killed"},{"bs":"i ubijeni su","en":"and they were killed"}],"ref":"2:72","answerWord":"قَتَلْتُمْ","answerSound":"audio/6f5ad1ff6f0e6fb45aac.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And (remember) when ye slew a man and disagreed concerning it and Allah brought forth that which ye were hiding.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَإِذْ","قَتَلْتُمْ","نَفْسًا","فَٱدَّٰرَْٰٔتُمْ","فِيهَا","وَٱللَّهُ","مُخْرِجٌ","مَّا","كُنتُمْ","تَكْتُمُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-154-3","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"biva ubijen","en":"he/it is killed"},{"bs":"ubijte!","en":"(you all) kill!"},{"bs":"ubijate ga","en":"you (all) kill him"},{"bs":"ubijeni smo","en":"we were killed"}],"ref":"2:154","answerWord":"يُقْتَلُ","answerSound":"audio/41f3de16832b4ac27ae1.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And call not those who are slain in the way of Allah \"dead.\" Nay, they are living, only ye perceive not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَلَا","تَقُولُوا۟","لِمَن","يُقْتَلُ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","أَمْوَٰتٌۢ","بَلْ","أَحْيَآءٌ","وَلَٰكِن","لَّا","تَشْعُرُونَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-191-21","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa ih ubijte!","en":"so (you all) kill them!"},{"bs":"ubijte!","en":"(you all) kill!"},{"bs":"ubijeni smo","en":"we were killed"},{"bs":"ubio sam","en":"I killed"}],"ref":"2:191","answerWord":"فَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/fcc0de32523ca0918c4f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And slay them wherever ye find them, and drive them out of the places whence they drove you out, for persecution is worse than slaughter. And fight not with them at the Inviolable Place of Worship until they first attack you there, but if they attack you (there) then slay them. Such is the reward of disbelievers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","حَيْثُ","ثَقِفْتُمُوهُمْ","وَأَخْرِجُوهُم","مِّنْ","حَيْثُ","أَخْرَجُوكُمْ","وَٱلْفِتْنَةُ","أَشَدُّ","مِنَ","ٱلْقَتْلِ","وَلَا","تُقَٰتِلُوهُمْ","عِندَ","ٱلْمَسْجِدِ","ٱلْحَرَامِ","حَتَّىٰ","يُقَٰتِلُوكُمْ","فِيهِ","فَإِن","قَٰتَلُوكُمْ","فَٱقْتُلُوهُمْ","كَذَٰلِكَ","جَزَآءُ","ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ"],"marked":[21],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-2-251-3","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"i ubio je","en":"and he/it killed"},{"bs":"zaista ću te ubiti","en":"surely I will kill you"},{"bs":"ubio si","en":"you killed"},{"bs":"ubijate","en":"you (all) kill"}],"ref":"2:251","answerWord":"وَقَتَلَ","answerSound":"audio/7a4b393732bff359dedf.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"So they routed them by Allah's leave and David slew Goliath; and Allah gave him the kingdom and wisdom, and taught him of that which He willeth. And if Allah had not repelled some men by others the earth would have been corrupted. But Allah is a Lord of Kindness to (His) creatures.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["فَهَزَمُوهُم","بِإِذْنِ","ٱللَّهِ","وَقَتَلَ","دَاوُۥدُ","جَالُوتَ","وَءَاتَىٰهُ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلْمُلْكَ","وَٱلْحِكْمَةَ","وَعَلَّمَهُۥ","مِمَّا","يَشَآءُ","وَلَوْلَا","دَفْعُ","ٱللَّهِ","ٱلنَّاسَ","بَعْضَهُم","بِبَعْضٍ","لَّفَسَدَتِ","ٱلْأَرْضُ","وَلَٰكِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","ذُو","فَضْلٍ","عَلَى","ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-3-183-24","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubili ste ih","en":"you (all) killed them"},{"bs":"pa ubijte!","en":"so (you all) kill!"},{"bs":"ubija","en":"he/it kills"},{"bs":"ubijaju","en":"they kill"}],"ref":"3:183","answerWord":"قَتَلْتُمُوهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/9bf9821e83895ce19b7d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(The same are) those who say: Lo! Allah hath charged us that we believe not in any messenger until he bring us an offering which fire (from heaven) shall devour. Say (unto them, O Muhammad): Messengers came unto you before me with miracles, and with that (very miracle) which ye describe. Why then did ye slay them? (Answer that) if ye are truthful!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["ٱلَّذِينَ","قَالُوٓا۟","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","عَهِدَ","إِلَيْنَآ","أَلَّا","نُؤْمِنَ","لِرَسُولٍ","حَتَّىٰ","يَأْتِيَنَا","بِقُرْبَانٍ","تَأْكُلُهُ","ٱلنَّارُ","قُلْ","قَدْ","جَآءَكُمْ","رُسُلٌ","مِّن","قَبْلِى","بِٱلْبَيِّنَٰتِ","وَبِٱلَّذِى","قُلْتُمْ","فَلِمَ","قَتَلْتُمُوهُمْ","إِن","كُنتُمْ","صَٰدِقِينَ"],"marked":[24],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-4-74-14","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"pa biva ubijen","en":"so he/it is killed"},{"bs":"da te ubiju","en":"so that they may kill you"},{"bs":"i ubio si","en":"and you killed"},{"bs":"i ubijeni su","en":"and they were killed"}],"ref":"4:74","answerWord":"فَيُقْتَلْ","answerSound":"audio/3915cfd6241c4807cd44.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Let those fight in the way of Allah who sell the life of this world for the other. Whoso fighteth in the way of Allah, be he slain or be he victorious, on him We shall bestow a vast reward.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["فَلْيُقَٰتِلْ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَشْرُونَ","ٱلْحَيَوٰةَ","ٱلدُّنْيَا","بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ","وَمَن","يُقَٰتِلْ","فِى","سَبِيلِ","ٱللَّهِ","فَيُقْتَلْ","أَوْ","يَغْلِبْ","فَسَوْفَ","نُؤْتِيهِ","أَجْرًا","عَظِيمًا"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-4-93-1","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubija","en":"he/it kills"},{"bs":"ubijeni su","en":"they were killed"},{"bs":"pa ga je ubio","en":"and he killed him"},{"bs":"ubili su ga","en":"they killed him"}],"ref":"4:93","answerWord":"يَقْتُلْ","answerSound":"audio/3ec15fcbd014d2b056e6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Whoso slayeth a believer of set purpose, his reward is hell for ever. Allah is wroth against him and He hath cursed him and prepared for him an awful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَمَن","يَقْتُلْ","مُؤْمِنًا","مُّتَعَمِّدًا","فَجَزَآؤُهُۥ","جَهَنَّمُ","خَٰلِدًا","فِيهَا","وَغَضِبَ","ٱللَّهُ","عَلَيْهِ","وَلَعَنَهُۥ","وَأَعَدَّ","لَهُۥ","عَذَابًا","عَظِيمًا"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-5-27-17","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"zaista ću te ubiti","en":"surely I will kill you"},{"bs":"pa biva ubijen","en":"so he/it is killed"},{"bs":"ubijeni ste","en":"you (all) were killed"},{"bs":"ubijen je","en":"he/it was killed"}],"ref":"5:27","answerWord":"لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ","answerSound":"audio/75b22a420f237a0ff335.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"But recite unto them with truth the tale of the two sons of Adam, how they offered each a sacrifice, and it was accepted from the one of them and it was not accepted from the other. (The one) said: I will surely kill thee. (The other) answered: Allah accepteth only from those who ward off (evil).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["وَٱتْلُ","عَلَيْهِمْ","نَبَأَ","ٱبْنَىْ","ءَادَمَ","بِٱلْحَقِّ","إِذْ","قَرَّبَا","قُرْبَانًا","فَتُقُبِّلَ","مِنْ","أَحَدِهِمَا","وَلَمْ","يُتَقَبَّلْ","مِنَ","ٱلْءَاخَرِ","قَالَ","لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ","قَالَ","إِنَّمَا","يَتَقَبَّلُ","ٱللَّهُ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُتَّقِينَ"],"marked":[17],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-5-28-10","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"da te ubijem","en":"so that I may kill you"},{"bs":"ubili ste ih","en":"you (all) killed them"},{"bs":"da te ubiju","en":"so that they may kill you"},{"bs":"ubili su ga","en":"they killed him"}],"ref":"5:28","answerWord":"لِأَقْتُلَكَ","answerSound":"audio/99d743563042908f3f8a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Even if thou stretch out thy hand against me to kill me, I shall not stretch out my hand against thee to kill thee, lo! I fear Allah, the Lord of the Worlds.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["لَئِنۢ","بَسَطتَ","إِلَىَّ","يَدَكَ","لِتَقْتُلَنِى","مَآ","أَنَا۠","بِبَاسِطٍ","يَدِىَ","إِلَيْكَ","لِأَقْتُلَكَ","إِنِّىٓ","أَخَافُ","ٱللَّهَ","رَبَّ","ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ"],"marked":[10],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-6-140-3","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubili su","en":"they killed"},{"bs":"ubit će me","en":"they will kill me"},{"bs":"ubijate","en":"you (all) kill"},{"bs":"ubija","en":"he/it kills"}],"ref":"6:140","answerWord":"قَتَلُوٓا۟","answerSound":"audio/a4b1019c5a31a9bb427a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They are losers who besottedly have slain their children without knowledge, and have forbidden that which Allah bestowed upon them, inventing a lie against Allah. They indeed have gone astray and are not guided.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["قَدْ","خَسِرَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","قَتَلُوٓا۟","أَوْلَٰدَهُمْ","سَفَهًۢا","بِغَيْرِ","عِلْمٍ","وَحَرَّمُوا۟","مَا","رَزَقَهُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱفْتِرَآءً","عَلَى","ٱللَّهِ","قَدْ","ضَلُّوا۟","وَمَا","كَانُوا۟","مُهْتَدِينَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"qatala-8-17-1","words":["verb:qatala"],"options":[{"bs":"ubijate ih","en":"you (all) kill them"},{"bs":"ubit će me","en":"they will kill me"},{"bs":"zar ubijate?","en":"do you (all) kill?"},{"bs":"ubili su","en":"they killed"}],"ref":"8:17","answerWord":"تَقْتُلُوهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/0bbfae73ceddf0226449.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Ye (Muslims) slew them not, but Allah slew them. And thou (Muhammad) threwest not when thou didst throw, but Allah threw, that He might test the believers by a fair test from Him. Lo! Allah is Hearer, Knower.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"ubiti","en":"to kill"},"passage":["فَلَمْ","تَقْتُلُوهُمْ","وَلَٰكِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","قَتَلَهُمْ","وَمَا","رَمَيْتَ","إِذْ","رَمَيْتَ","وَلَٰكِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","رَمَىٰ","وَلِيُبْلِىَ","ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","مِنْهُ","بَلَآءً","حَسَنًا","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","سَمِيعٌ","عَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"قَتَلَ"}},{"id":"hakama-22-69-1","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"},{"bs":"(Allah je) presudio","en":"(God has) judged"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you (all) judge"}],"ref":"22:69","answerWord":"يَحْكُمُ","answerSound":"audio/3405227a8fe01534a43d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection concerning that wherein ye used to differ.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["ٱللَّهُ","يَحْكُمُ","بَيْنَكُمْ","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","فِيمَا","كُنتُمْ","فِيهِ","تَخْتَلِفُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-5-42-6","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"pa sudi!","en":"so judge!"},{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you (all) judge"},{"bs":"sude","en":"they judge"}],"ref":"5:42","answerWord":"فَٱحْكُم","answerSound":"audio/875845f2737513a1f2d7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Listeners for the sake of falsehood! Greedy for illicit gain! If then they have recourse unto thee (Muhammad) judge between them or disclaim jurisdiction. If thou disclaimest jurisdiction, then they cannot harm thee at all. But if thou judgest, judge between them with equity. Lo! Allah loveth the equitable.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["سَمَّٰعُونَ","لِلْكَذِبِ","أَكَّٰلُونَ","لِلسُّحْتِ","فَإِن","جَآءُوكَ","فَٱحْكُم","بَيْنَهُمْ","أَوْ","أَعْرِضْ","عَنْهُمْ","وَإِن","تُعْرِضْ","عَنْهُمْ","فَلَن","يَضُرُّوكَ","شَيْـًٔا","وَإِنْ","حَكَمْتَ","فَٱحْكُم","بَيْنَهُم","بِٱلْقِسْطِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يُحِبُّ","ٱلْمُقْسِطِينَ"],"marked":[6,19],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-29-4-9","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sude","en":"they judge"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you judge"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"},{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"}],"ref":"29:4","answerWord":"يَحْكُمُونَ","answerSound":"audio/35e420eb5d6096a60e55.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Or do those who do ill-deeds imagine that they can outstrip Us? Evil (for them) is that which they decide.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["أَمْ","حَسِبَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَعْمَلُونَ","ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ","أَن","يَسْبِقُونَا","سَآءَ","مَا","يَحْكُمُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-37-154-3","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudite","en":"you judge"},{"bs":"sude","en":"they judge"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"i neka sudi","en":"and let him judge"}],"ref":"37:154","answerWord":"تَحْكُمُونَ","answerSound":"audio/f8ec676b3ec717171f2c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"What aileth you? How judge ye?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["مَا","لَكُمْ","كَيْفَ","تَحْكُمُونَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-7-87-13","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"},{"bs":"sudio si","en":"you judged"},{"bs":"sude","en":"they (two) judge"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"}],"ref":"7:87","answerWord":"يَحْكُمَ","answerSound":"audio/9bcc9b687296a3662a0d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if there is a party of you which believeth in that wherewith I have been sent, and there is a party which believeth not, then have patience until Allah judge between us. He is the Best of all who deal in judgment.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["وَإِن","كَانَ","طَآئِفَةٌ","مِّنكُمْ","ءَامَنُوا۟","بِٱلَّذِىٓ","أُرْسِلْتُ","بِهِۦ","وَطَآئِفَةٌ","لَّمْ","يُؤْمِنُوا۟","فَٱصْبِرُوا۟","حَتَّىٰ","يَحْكُمَ","ٱللَّهُ","بَيْنَنَا","وَهُوَ","خَيْرُ","ٱلْحَٰكِمِينَ"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-21-112-2","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudi!","en":"judge!"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you (all) judge"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"},{"bs":"da sudi","en":"so that he/it may judge"}],"ref":"21:112","answerWord":"ٱحْكُم","answerSound":"audio/28207764a7dec7054809.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He saith: My Lord! Judge Thou with truth. Our Lord is the Beneficent, Whose help is to be implored against that which ye ascribe (unto Him).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["قَٰلَ","رَبِّ","ٱحْكُم","بِٱلْحَقِّ","وَرَبُّنَا","ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ","ٱلْمُسْتَعَانُ","عَلَىٰ","مَا","تَصِفُونَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-3-55-24","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"},{"bs":"sudio si","en":"you judged"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you judge"}],"ref":"3:55","answerWord":"فَأَحْكُمُ","answerSound":"audio/0277ac42c96d2cbaa02e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"(And remember) when Allah said: O Jesus! Lo! I am gathering thee and causing thee to ascend unto Me, and am cleansing thee of those who disbelieve and am setting those who follow thee above those who disbelieve until the Day of Resurrection. Then unto Me ye will (all) return, and I shall judge between you as to that wherein ye used to differ.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["إِذْ","قَالَ","ٱللَّهُ","يَٰعِيسَىٰٓ","إِنِّى","مُتَوَفِّيكَ","وَرَافِعُكَ","إِلَىَّ","وَمُطَهِّرُكَ","مِنَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","وَجَاعِلُ","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱتَّبَعُوكَ","فَوْقَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوٓا۟","إِلَىٰ","يَوْمِ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","ثُمَّ","إِلَىَّ","مَرْجِعُكُمْ","فَأَحْكُمُ","بَيْنَكُمْ","فِيمَا","كُنتُمْ","فِيهِ","تَخْتَلِفُونَ"],"marked":[24],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-4-58-9","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"sudio si","en":"you judged"},{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"}],"ref":"4:58","answerWord":"حَكَمْتُم","answerSound":"audio/383b4fec5dc4aeaf502b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! Allah commandeth you that ye restore deposits to their owners, and, if ye judge between mankind, that ye judge justly. Lo! comely is this which Allah admonisheth you. Lo! Allah is ever Hearer, Seer.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يَأْمُرُكُمْ","أَن","تُؤَدُّوا۟","ٱلْأَمَٰنَٰتِ","إِلَىٰٓ","أَهْلِهَا","وَإِذَا","حَكَمْتُم","بَيْنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","أَن","تَحْكُمُوا۟","بِٱلْعَدْلِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","نِعِمَّا","يَعِظُكُم","بِهِۦٓ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","كَانَ","سَمِيعًۢا","بَصِيرًا"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-4-58-13","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudite","en":"you (all) judge"},{"bs":"sudi","en":"he/it judges"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"pa sudi!","en":"so judge!"}],"ref":"4:58","answerWord":"تَحْكُمُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/0feb9f887d192d5ec998.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! Allah commandeth you that ye restore deposits to their owners, and, if ye judge between mankind, that ye judge justly. Lo! comely is this which Allah admonisheth you. Lo! Allah is ever Hearer, Seer.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يَأْمُرُكُمْ","أَن","تُؤَدُّوا۟","ٱلْأَمَٰنَٰتِ","إِلَىٰٓ","أَهْلِهَا","وَإِذَا","حَكَمْتُم","بَيْنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","أَن","تَحْكُمُوا۟","بِٱلْعَدْلِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","نِعِمَّا","يَعِظُكُم","بِهِۦٓ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","كَانَ","سَمِيعًۢا","بَصِيرًا"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-5-42-18","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"sudio si","en":"you judged"},{"bs":"sude","en":"they judge"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"sudite","en":"you judge"}],"ref":"5:42","answerWord":"حَكَمْتَ","answerSound":"audio/136477c0d2a413354d08.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Listeners for the sake of falsehood! Greedy for illicit gain! If then they have recourse unto thee (Muhammad) judge between them or disclaim jurisdiction. If thou disclaimest jurisdiction, then they cannot harm thee at all. But if thou judgest, judge between them with equity. Lo! Allah loveth the equitable.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["سَمَّٰعُونَ","لِلْكَذِبِ","أَكَّٰلُونَ","لِلسُّحْتِ","فَإِن","جَآءُوكَ","فَٱحْكُم","بَيْنَهُمْ","أَوْ","أَعْرِضْ","عَنْهُمْ","وَإِن","تُعْرِضْ","عَنْهُمْ","فَلَن","يَضُرُّوكَ","شَيْـًٔا","وَإِنْ","حَكَمْتَ","فَٱحْكُم","بَيْنَهُم","بِٱلْقِسْطِ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","يُحِبُّ","ٱلْمُقْسِطِينَ"],"marked":[18],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-5-47-0","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"i neka sudi","en":"and let him judge"},{"bs":"(Allah je) presudio","en":"(God has) judged"},{"bs":"sudili ste","en":"you (all) judged"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"}],"ref":"5:47","answerWord":"وَلْيَحْكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/30776ac21f76e6464f73.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Let the People of the Gospel judge by that which Allah hath revealed therein. Whoso judgeth not by that which Allah hath revealed: such are evil-livers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["وَلْيَحْكُمْ","أَهْلُ","ٱلْإِنجِيلِ","بِمَآ","أَنزَلَ","ٱللَّهُ","فِيهِ","وَمَن","لَّمْ","يَحْكُم","بِمَآ","أَنزَلَ","ٱللَّهُ","فَأُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","هُمُ","ٱلْفَٰسِقُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-16-124-9","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"zaista sudi","en":"surely he/it judges"},{"bs":"pa sudim","en":"so I judge"},{"bs":"pa sudi!","en":"so judge!"},{"bs":"(Allah je) presudio","en":"(God has) judged"}],"ref":"16:124","answerWord":"لَيَحْكُمُ","answerSound":"audio/df34bf7341facd9c9b93.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The Sabbath was appointed only for those who differed concerning it, and lo! thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection concerning that wherein they used to differ.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["إِنَّمَا","جُعِلَ","ٱلسَّبْتُ","عَلَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱخْتَلَفُوا۟","فِيهِ","وَإِنَّ","رَبَّكَ","لَيَحْكُمُ","بَيْنَهُمْ","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","فِيمَا","كَانُوا۟","فِيهِ","يَخْتَلِفُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"hakama-40-48-9","words":["verb:hakama"],"options":[{"bs":"(Allah je) presudio","en":"(God has) judged"},{"bs":"pa sudi!","en":"so judge!"},{"bs":"i neka sudi","en":"and let him judge"},{"bs":"sudio si","en":"you judged"}],"ref":"40:48","answerWord":"حَكَمَ","answerSound":"audio/c0eb7cb54816a60e6a87.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Those who were proud say: Lo! we are all (together) herein. Lo! Allah hath judged between (His) slaves.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"suditi, presuditi","en":"to judge, to rule"},"passage":["قَالَ","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱسْتَكْبَرُوٓا۟","إِنَّا","كُلٌّ","فِيهَآ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","قَدْ","حَكَمَ","بَيْنَ","ٱلْعِبَادِ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"حَكَمَ"}},{"id":"malaka-23-6-5","words":["verb:malaka"],"options":[{"bs":"posjeduju","en":"possess"},{"bs":"posjedujete","en":"you (all) own"},{"bs":"posjedovali ste","en":"you (all) owned"},{"bs":"posjedujem","en":"I possess"}],"ref":"23:6","answerWord":"مَلَكَتْ","answerSound":"audio/ee6f95238d93a7e27eb5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Save from their wives or the (slaves) that their right hands possess, for then they are not blameworthy,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"posjedovati, imati u vlasti","en":"to own, to possess"},"passage":["إِلَّا","عَلَىٰٓ","أَزْوَٰجِهِمْ","أَوْ","مَا","مَلَكَتْ","أَيْمَٰنُهُمْ","فَإِنَّهُمْ","غَيْرُ","مَلُومِينَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"مَلَكَ"}},{"id":"malaka-19-87-1","words":["verb:malaka"],"options":[{"bs":"posjeduju","en":"they own"},{"bs":"posjedovali ste","en":"you (all) owned"},{"bs":"posjeduje","en":"he/it owns"},{"bs":"posjedujem","en":"I possess"}],"ref":"19:87","answerWord":"يَمْلِكُونَ","answerSound":"audio/285cc8f9501ccef37a06.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They will have no power of intercession, save him who hath made a covenant with his Lord.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"posjedovati, imati u vlasti","en":"to own, to possess"},"passage":["لَّا","يَمْلِكُونَ","ٱلشَّفَٰعَةَ","إِلَّا","مَنِ","ٱتَّخَذَ","عِندَ","ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ","عَهْدًا"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"مَلَكَ"}},{"id":"malaka-20-89-7","words":["verb:malaka"],"options":[{"bs":"posjeduje","en":"he/it owns"},{"bs":"posjedujem","en":"I possess"},{"bs":"posjeduju","en":"possess"},{"bs":"posjedovali ste","en":"you (all) owned"}],"ref":"20:89","answerWord":"يَمْلِكُ","answerSound":"audio/a9a86861736c971f4392.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"See they not, then, that it returneth no saying unto them and possesseth for them neither hurt nor use?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"posjedovati, imati u vlasti","en":"to own, to possess"},"passage":["أَفَلَا","يَرَوْنَ","أَلَّا","يَرْجِعُ","إِلَيْهِمْ","قَوْلًا","وَلَا","يَمْلِكُ","لَهُمْ","ضَرًّا","وَلَا","نَفْعًا"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"مَلَكَ"}},{"id":"malaka-72-21-3","words":["verb:malaka"],"options":[{"bs":"posjedujem","en":"I possess"},{"bs":"posjedovali ste","en":"you (all) owned"},{"bs":"posjedujete","en":"you (all) own"},{"bs":"posjeduje","en":"he/it owns"}],"ref":"72:21","answerWord":"أَمْلِكُ","answerSound":"audio/5655803fb44a618fbeba.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: Lo! I control not hurt nor benefit for you.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"posjedovati, imati u vlasti","en":"to own, to possess"},"passage":["قُلْ","إِنِّى","لَآ","أَمْلِكُ","لَكُمْ","ضَرًّا","وَلَا","رَشَدًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"مَلَكَ"}},{"id":"malaka-17-100-3","words":["verb:malaka"],"options":[{"bs":"posjedujete","en":"you (all) own"},{"bs":"posjedovali ste","en":"you (all) owned"},{"bs":"posjeduje","en":"he/it owns"},{"bs":"posjeduju","en":"possess"}],"ref":"17:100","answerWord":"تَمْلِكُونَ","answerSound":"audio/dd5e3c212018216c7a74.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say (unto them): If ye possessed the treasures of the mercy of my Lord, ye would surely hold them back for fear of spending, for man was ever grudging.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"posjedovati, imati u vlasti","en":"to own, to possess"},"passage":["قُل","لَّوْ","أَنتُمْ","تَمْلِكُونَ","خَزَآئِنَ","رَحْمَةِ","رَبِّىٓ","إِذًا","لَّأَمْسَكْتُمْ","خَشْيَةَ","ٱلْإِنفَاقِ","وَكَانَ","ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ","قَتُورًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"مَلَكَ"}},{"id":"akhadha-2-2-225-1","words":["verb:akhadha-2"],"options":[{"bs":"kažnjava vas","en":"he/it takes you (all) to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava ih","en":"he/it takes them to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava","en":"he/it takes to task"},{"bs":"ne kori me","en":"do not blame me"}],"ref":"2:225","answerWord":"يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ","answerSound":"audio/c1d5f97d57150acfcf23.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah will not take you to task for that which is unintentional in your oaths. But He will take you to task for that which your hearts have garnered. Allah is Forgiving, Clement.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"kazniti, pozvati na odgovornost","en":"to blame, to hold accountable"},"passage":["لَّا","يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","بِٱللَّغْوِ","فِىٓ","أَيْمَٰنِكُمْ","وَلَٰكِن","يُؤَاخِذُكُم","بِمَا","كَسَبَتْ","قُلُوبُكُمْ","وَٱللَّهُ","غَفُورٌ","حَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"آخَذَ"}},{"id":"akhadha-2-2-225-7","words":["verb:akhadha-2"],"options":[{"bs":"kažnjava vas","en":"he/it takes you (all) to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava ih","en":"he/it takes them to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava","en":"he/it takes to task"},{"bs":"ne kori me","en":"do not blame me"}],"ref":"2:225","answerWord":"يُؤَاخِذُكُم","answerSound":"audio/39e5d96c96f31771f460.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah will not take you to task for that which is unintentional in your oaths. But He will take you to task for that which your hearts have garnered. Allah is Forgiving, Clement.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"kazniti, pozvati na odgovornost","en":"to blame, to hold accountable"},"passage":["لَّا","يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","بِٱللَّغْوِ","فِىٓ","أَيْمَٰنِكُمْ","وَلَٰكِن","يُؤَاخِذُكُم","بِمَا","كَسَبَتْ","قُلُوبُكُمْ","وَٱللَّهُ","غَفُورٌ","حَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"آخَذَ"}},{"id":"akhadha-2-16-61-1","words":["verb:akhadha-2"],"options":[{"bs":"kažnjava","en":"he/it takes to task"},{"bs":"ne kori me","en":"do not blame me"},{"bs":"kažnjava ih","en":"he/it takes them to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava vas","en":"he/it takes you (all) to task"}],"ref":"16:61","answerWord":"يُؤَاخِذُ","answerSound":"audio/fb86da076e36cb614ad9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"If Allah were to take mankind to task for their wrong-doing, he would not leave hereon a living creature, but He reprieveth them to an appointed term, and when their term cometh they cannot put (it) off an hour nor (yet) advance (it).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"kazniti, pozvati na odgovornost","en":"to blame, to hold accountable"},"passage":["وَلَوْ","يُؤَاخِذُ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلنَّاسَ","بِظُلْمِهِم","مَّا","تَرَكَ","عَلَيْهَا","مِن","دَآبَّةٍ","وَلَٰكِن","يُؤَخِّرُهُمْ","إِلَىٰٓ","أَجَلٍ","مُّسَمًّى","فَإِذَا","جَآءَ","أَجَلُهُمْ","لَا","يَسْتَـْٔخِرُونَ","سَاعَةً","وَلَا","يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"آخَذَ"}},{"id":"akhadha-2-18-58-5","words":["verb:akhadha-2"],"options":[{"bs":"kažnjava ih","en":"he/it takes them to task"},{"bs":"ne kori me","en":"do not blame me"},{"bs":"kažnjava","en":"he/it takes to task"},{"bs":"kažnjava vas","en":"he/it takes you (all) to task"}],"ref":"18:58","answerWord":"يُؤَاخِذُهُم","answerSound":"audio/0eaba1a89f160ae448d3.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Thy Lord is the Forgiver, Full of Mercy. If He took them to task (now) for what they earn, He would hasten on the doom for them; but theirs is an appointed term from which they will find no escape.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"kazniti, pozvati na odgovornost","en":"to blame, to hold accountable"},"passage":["وَرَبُّكَ","ٱلْغَفُورُ","ذُو","ٱلرَّحْمَةِ","لَوْ","يُؤَاخِذُهُم","بِمَا","كَسَبُوا۟","لَعَجَّلَ","لَهُمُ","ٱلْعَذَابَ","بَل","لَّهُم","مَّوْعِدٌ","لَّن","يَجِدُوا۟","مِن","دُونِهِۦ","مَوْئِلًا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"آخَذَ"}},{"id":"tabia-2-38-9","words":["verb:tabia"],"options":[{"bs":"slijedio je","en":"he/it followed"},{"bs":"slijedili su","en":"they followed"},{"bs":"koju prati","en":"is followed by it"},{"bs":"slijedio me je","en":"he/it followed me"}],"ref":"2:38","answerWord":"تَبِعَ","answerSound":"audio/a12b4ba2390057e265f6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We said: Go down, all of you, from hence; but verily there cometh unto you from Me a guidance; and whoso followeth My guidance, there shall no fear come upon them neither shall they grieve.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"slijediti, pratiti","en":"to follow"},"passage":["قُلْنَا","ٱهْبِطُوا۟","مِنْهَا","جَمِيعًا","فَإِمَّا","يَأْتِيَنَّكُم","مِّنِّى","هُدًى","فَمَن","تَبِعَ","هُدَاىَ","فَلَا","خَوْفٌ","عَلَيْهِمْ","وَلَا","هُمْ","يَحْزَنُونَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"تَبِعَ"}},{"id":"tabia-2-263-6","words":["verb:tabia"],"options":[{"bs":"koju prati","en":"is followed by it"},{"bs":"slijedio me je","en":"he/it followed me"},{"bs":"slijedili su","en":"they followed"},{"bs":"slijedio je","en":"he/it followed"}],"ref":"2:263","answerWord":"يَتْبَعُهَآ","answerSound":"audio/39d4c46c9ceffe7456b3.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"A kind word with forgiveness is better than almsgiving followed by injury. Allah is Absolute, Clement.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"slijediti, pratiti","en":"to follow"},"passage":["قَوْلٌ","مَّعْرُوفٌ","وَمَغْفِرَةٌ","خَيْرٌ","مِّن","صَدَقَةٍ","يَتْبَعُهَآ","أَذًى","وَٱللَّهُ","غَنِىٌّ","حَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"تَبِعَ"}},{"id":"tabia-14-36-7","words":["verb:tabia"],"options":[{"bs":"slijedio me je","en":"he/it followed me"},{"bs":"slijedili su","en":"they followed"},{"bs":"slijedio je","en":"he/it followed"},{"bs":"koju prati","en":"is followed by it"}],"ref":"14:36","answerWord":"تَبِعَنِى","answerSound":"audio/cf18cde87297d81b8ec0.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"My Lord! Lo! they have led many of mankind astray. But whoso followeth me, he verily is of me. And whoso disobeyeth me - Still Thou art Forgiving, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"slijediti, pratiti","en":"to follow"},"passage":["رَبِّ","إِنَّهُنَّ","أَضْلَلْنَ","كَثِيرًا","مِّنَ","ٱلنَّاسِ","فَمَن","تَبِعَنِى","فَإِنَّهُۥ","مِنِّى","وَمَنْ","عَصَانِى","فَإِنَّكَ","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"تَبِعَ"}}]